-D-glucose and open chain D-glucose open chain D-glucose","open chain D-glucose","mixture of $\\alpha$-D-glucose and $\\beta$-D-glucose"],"answer":3,"solution":"<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FD_vu0AguaP8D8IH9lRI2z7Vu6DPIT5wkvj84Aswszqo.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FD_vu0AguaP8D8IH9lRI2z7Vu6DPIT5wkvj84Aswszqo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2FD_vu0AguaP8D8IH9lRI2z7Vu6DPIT5wkvj84Aswszqo.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\">","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2015 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213fc5dba4d88c558f6"},{"id":50965,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"In the DNA of E. Coli the mole ratio of adenine to cytosine is $0.7$. If the number of moles of adenine in the DNA is 350000 , the number of moles of guanine is equal to -","options":["350000","500000","225000","700000"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\begin{array}{l}\n\\frac{A}{C}=0.7 \\\\\n\\frac{35 \\times 10^{4}}{C}=0.7 \\\\\nC=\\frac{35 \\times 10^{4}}{0.7}=5 \\times 10^{5}\n\\end{array}$\nMoles of cytosine $=$ moles of guanine","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2012 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2137e2422cf19ab8d93"},{"id":50966,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"<p>The average energy of each hydrogen bond in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> pair is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo> </mo><mi>kcal</mi></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and that in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> pair is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo> </mo><msup><mi>kcalmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assuming that no other interaction exists between the nucleotides, the approximate energy required in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>kcalmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> to split the following double stranded <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DNA</mi></math> into two single strands is<br/>\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252F33fc4e58-c159-4c91-91fa-7a75ed5eac80-image.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2F33fc4e58-c159-4c91-91fa-7a75ed5eac80-image.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fkvpy%2F33fc4e58-c159-4c91-91fa-7a75ed5eac80-image.png?alt=media\"/><br/>\n[Each dashed line may represent more than one hydrogen bond between the base pairs]</p>","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonds in each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>Number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonds in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p>\n\n<p>The given double stranded <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DNA</mi></math> has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> pairs.</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math> Total number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonds in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> pair<br />\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>Total number of H-bonds in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> pair<br />\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo></math> Average energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math>-bonds in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>.</p>\n\n<p>Average energy of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> -bonds in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> pair <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math></p>\n\n<p>Thus, the approximate energy required to split the double stranded <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>DNA</mi></math> in two single strands <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da692d8fdd1a3eea47faa"},{"id":50967,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Biomolecules","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The reaction of D-glucose with ammoniacal $\\mathrm{AgNO}_{3}$ produces","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Fkvpy%252FcxFm7Oi5vg5oxsREY6Y0JS9grI6Tn-WGAquEK-OOOgk.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebas